    <string name="app_text_catalog_247" formatted="false">Monitoring information</string>
    <string name="app_text_catalog_248" formatted="false">Monitoring is opt-in and uses a motion heuristic. It can miss falls or flag ordinary movement; it is not medical-grade and cannot replace emergency services.</string>
    <string name="app_text_catalog_249" formatted="false">Android may ask for Activity Recognition permission to run this health foreground service. Sensor readings stay on this device.</string>
    <string name="app_text_catalog_250" formatted="false">Android background limits</string>
    <string name="app_text_catalog_251" formatted="false">Start monitoring while this screen is visible. Android keeps it in a foreground service with a permanent notification. MedMitra does not restart sensor monitoring after reboot; turn it on again after a restart.</string>
    <string name="app_text_catalog_252" formatted="false">Accelerometer, gyroscope, and fused orientation data are processed locally when those sensors are available. MedMitra does not request background location or body-sensor access for this feature.</string>
    <string name="app_text_catalog_253" formatted="false">Battery optimization exemption: allowed</string>
    <string name="app_text_catalog_254" formatted="false">Battery optimization: Android or the phone maker may pause the service under heavy restrictions. Review system battery settings if monitoring stops.</string>
    <string name="app_text_catalog_255" formatted="false">Lower sensitivity reduces false alarms but may miss events. Higher sensitivity may trigger more often. New settings apply immediately if monitoring is active.</string>
    <string name="app_text_catalog_256" formatted="false">A motion candidate shows a notification with an “I’m okay” cancel action. If it expires, MedMitra records it and offers SOS. It never sends a message or places a call automatically.</string>
